#: sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn:182
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanClose: end the bean in a state that says why — complete and archive it, scrap it with its reasons and archive it, or record the blocker and hand it back. The one place resolve and archive are drawn (bean m8gz, owner 2026-10-24); placed straight before the end so the engine's resolve sees nothing left but the archive step."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn:166
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanOpen: check before you create, find out whose the bean is, and claim it — or leave it alone when it is someone else's. The one place a claim is drawn (bean m8gz, owner 2026-10-24); the gateway after this reads which end it reached."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn:133
#. Diagram label
msgid "Re-enter a train on the new head"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn:172
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Reads which end Process_BeanOpen reached. `claimed`: the bean is in progress and this process works it. `not yours`: a sibling session or a human holds it, nothing was written to it, and this process stops here rather than work a bean it does not own (bean-coordination)."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn:146
#. Diagram label
msgid "Record the merge commit as evidence"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn:61
#. Diagram label
msgid "Record the refusal on the bean"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn:204
#. Diagram label
msgid "refused again"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn:156
#. Diagram label
msgid "Scrap the bean, with the reason"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn:178
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Someone else holds the bean; this run stops without touching it."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn:84
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The `agent-handoff` format (#1884): Roles, Report to (the PR), Done when, Fails if. The fail condition: no `started` line within 4 h, no push within 24 h, the session gone, or `blocked` on something it cannot settle. One line to the session; the instructions are in the bean."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn:157
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The agent's own `beans update --status scrapped`; never deleted."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn:134
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The next train is the verifier: the executor's own log is evidence, not the close."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn:62
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The PR, the head sha the train used, the train and its other members, each refused path or failing gate and why. A repeat refusal goes under `## Attempts` with `--body-append`."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn:140
#. Diagram label
msgid "The PR's fate?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn:47
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The session named in the PR's `Claude-Session:` trailer. The executor of the hand-back: claims the refusal bean, fixes the PR, reports on the PR in the bean's one-line formats."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn:120
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Two siblings editing one bean, one script changed differently on both sides, a budget exceeded only in combination: each is a choice between authors."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn:212
#. Diagram label
msgid "waiting on the owner"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn:130
#. Diagram label
msgid "Waiting on the owner's ruling"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn:18
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "What a merge steward does with a PR it dropped from a merge train: its merge (`merge-base.bpmn`, run with `--no-regen`) refused an authored or undeclared conflict, or the train's combined result failed a gate. Owner, 2026-10-02: \"create a new bean (under appropriate epic/story…), hand it back to the sibling (use the agent-to-agent handoff process with a fail condition) for resolution, or dispatch an agent as appropriate.\" Bean `zacz`; the discipline is in `merge-conflict-patterns` §\"When a merge-train member is refused\". ONE INSTANCE PER REFUSED PR, started with `bean:` set to the refusal bean. The steward finds or creates that bean BEFORE starting the instance, because creating a bean is the agent's own `beans create` call, deduplicated by the PR number in its title; the engine has no create op (`bean-lifecycle.bpmn`). A second refusal of the same PR loops back into this instance rather than opening a second bean."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn:186
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Which outcome the bean was closed with, so each ends at its own named end event. The bean is closed once, on every path (bpmn-authoring: open and close the bean at the top, once)."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn:191
#. Diagram label
msgid "yes"
msgstr ""
